+# Current Attributes → Explicit Execution Context
 
 ## Summary
 
-`Current` is Rails' built-in thread-local storage for request-scoped context like current user, tenant, or request metadata. It enables implicit context passing but must be used carefully to avoid coupling layers.
+The original chapter separates execution context from domain state. Go has no request-local `Current` singleton: goroutines are not thread-local requests, and a package variable races across users. Carry business inputs explicitly.
 
 ## Layer Placement
 
-```
-┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
-│ Presentation Layer                      │
-│  └─ Sets Current values in controllers  │
-├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
-│ Application Layer                       │
-│  └─ May read Current (sparingly)        │
-├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
-│ Domain Layer                            │
-│  └─ Should NOT access Current           │
